-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat manufacturer from part P7 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P7-seat-manufacturer: THE SEAT LAYER for a product manufacturer that places an AI system on the market together with its product, over the layer-1 modules of Articles 57 to 71
-- of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744).
-- SEAT: the product manufacturer. In this part the text addresses "providers or prospective providers of AI enabled products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I"
-- (Article 60a, inserted by the Omnibus): a manufacturer of such a product is the provider of the AI system that is part of it. The questions below are those a manufacturer of a Section B product would ask
-- about the Member State's real-world testing frameworks. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls one layer-1 function.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, one of the keel's own choices, each with an @desc. The date asked comes first. `General` applies from 2 August 2026.
-- The role question that the plan assigns to this seat (`Art 2(1)(e) the Regulation applies to the product manufacturer`) is written by another agent and is not asked here.
-- Article 2(2) is a call to the keel's `Art 2(2)`: the question on Article 60a asks the route, whether the products are covered by the Section B legislation and whether the requirements are integrated in it.
-- Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled). The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

§ `Under Article 57: the group General`

-- The applicability question for the provision group `General` that Article 57 opens in this part's range: it asks only the date, and passes the core's constants for the route, the placement date and the change.
@export Under Article 57, as a product manufacturer, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a product manufacturer, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `General` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)


§ `Under Article 60a: testing of AI-enabled products covered by Section B of Annex I in real world conditions`

-- Article 60a was inserted by the Omnibus and applies from 2 August 2026 as part of the group General. It is for high-risk AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I.

-- Article 60a(1): Member States may allow, in accordance with that Article, the testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside the sandboxes by providers or prospective providers of AI-enabled products covered by Section B of Annex I, to assess and verify conformity with Articles 8 to 15.
@export Under Article 60a, as a product manufacturer, may my Member State allow me to test my AI-enabled product in real world conditions outside an AI regulatory sandbox?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products to which your AI system relates covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation (the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I that covers the products)?
      `the testing is of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing is of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes? Answer yes or no.
      `the testing is by providers or prospective providers of AI enabled products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing is by providers or prospective providers of AI enabled products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer yes or no.
      `the testing is with a view to assessing and verifying the conformity of those systems with the requirements laid down in Articles 8 to 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing is with a view to assessing and verifying the conformity of those systems with the requirements laid down in Articles 8 to 15? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60a, as a product manufacturer, may my Member State allow me to test my AI-enabled product in real world conditions outside an AI regulatory sandbox` IS
    `Art 60a(1) the Member State may allow the testing outside the sandboxes of AI-enabled products covered by Section B of Annex I` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the testing is of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes` `the testing is by providers or prospective providers of AI enabled products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the testing is with a view to assessing and verifying the conformity of those systems with the requirements laid down in Articles 8 to 15`

